{"book":{"id":"book-bond-of-iron-master-and-slave-at-buffalo-forge-charles-b-dew","slug":"bond-of-iron-master-and-slave-at-buffalo-forge-charles-b-dew","title":"Bond of Iron: Master and Slave at Buffalo Forge","authors":[{"id":"person-charles-b-dew","name":"Charles B. Dew"}],"isbn13":["9780393313598"],"subjects":["History"],"topics":["Slavery & Emancipation","Black History & Culture","Gender & Feminism","War & Military Strategy"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Bond%20of%20Iron%3A%20Master%20and%20Slave%20at%20Buffalo%20Forge%20Charles%20B.%20Dew","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Bond%20of%20Iron%3A%20Master%20and%20Slave%20at%20Buffalo%20Forge%20Charles%20B.%20Dew","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Bond%20of%20Iron%3A%20Master%20and%20Slave%20at%20Buffalo%20Forge%20Charles%20B.%20Dew","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Bond%20of%20Iron%3A%20Master%20and%20Slave%20at%20Buffalo%20Forge%20Charles%20B.%20Dew","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL3907672W"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-lincoln-prize-civil-war-era-gettysburg-college-previous-winners-of-the-gilder-lehrman-lincoln-pr","source-open-library-bond-of-iron-master-and-slave-at-buffalo-forge-charles-b-dew","source-open-library-summary-bond-of-iron-master-and-slave-at-buffalo-forge-charles-b-dew"],"publicationYear":1994,"thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/248989-L.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":37,"criticalRenown":72,"controversy":18,"llmAffinity":78,"affinityResidual":1.71,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.91,"criticalRenown":0.9,"controversy":0.78,"llmAffinity":0.96},"tags":{"craft":"craft-of-explanation","evidence":"archival-research","stance":"moral-seriousness"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"summary":"The records dealing with the Buffalo Forge slaves are unique in their completeness; never before have details of this life in the American South been so rich, so exacting, and so accessible to historian and general reader alike. Historian Charles Dew's exhaustive study of the Buffalo Forge asks - to use Charles Joyner's wonderful phrase - \"large questions in small places\"; he describes what working and living conditions were like for the slave artisans and their families, traces patterns of accommodation and resistance, and elucidates the complex interaction between white and black that constituted the inner core of the master-slave relationship. Buffalo Forge was an extensive ironmaking and farming enterprise located approximately nine miles southeast of Lexington in the Valley of Virginia. This property was developed in the antebellum period by two men: William Weaver, a Pennsylvania entrepreneur who made his initial investment at Buffalo Forge during the War of 1812, and Daniel C. E. Brady, another Pennsylvanian and a relative of Weaver's whom Weaver brought down to the valley during the 1850s to assist him in managing the Buffalo Forge operations.","subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"History","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-bond-of-iron-master-and-slave-at-buffalo-forge-charles-b-dew"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Race relations","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-bond-of-iron-master-and-slave-at-buffalo-forge-charles-b-dew"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Slave labor","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-bond-of-iron-master-and-slave-at-buffalo-forge-charles-b-dew"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Slaves","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-bond-of-iron-master-and-slave-at-buffalo-forge-charles-b-dew"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Social conditions","s